{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013uMgogox2vspHDUdHUciuH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# kingfisher\n2\t\n3\tA local, browser-based live view of a coding agent at work. A Rust daemon on 127.0.0.1 owns the\n4\tagent process, normalises its event stream, and feeds a WebGPU scene in a browser tab where one\n5\tcan watch, chat back, interrupt, and approve permission requests.\n6\t\n7\tRuns Claude Code first, by spawning the unmodified official `claude` binary under the user's own\n8\tlogin. kingfisher never reads, stores or forwards credentials. Other agents come later, through\n9\tadapters.\n10\t\n11\t## Status\n12\t\n13\tDesign only. No code yet.\n14\t\n15\t- [docs/design-report.md](docs/design-report.md) is the founding research report (2026-11-14):\n16\t  feasibility, integration paths, terms, prior art, rendering stack, architecture, MVP plan.\n17\t\n18\t## Plan\n19\t\n20\t| Milestone | Scope |\n21\t|---|---|\n22\t| Weekend MVP | Daemon spawns `claude -p` in bidirectional stream-json; `PermissionRequest` HTTP hook for approvals; cosmic scene, transcript panel, chat, interrupt; NDJSON archive and replay |\n23\t| v0.2 | Global hooks plus transcript tail to observe hand-started sessions; take over via `--resume`; timeline, diff view, terminal pane, sonification; hang watchdog |\n24\t| v0.3 | ACP and Codex adapters; multi-session; more themes; optional OTLP receiver |\n25\t\n26\t## Before any public release\n27\t\n28\tRe-read Anthropic's Claude Code legal page. The design relies on its carve-out for an end user\n29\tsigning in to the unmodified binary with their own subscription, and that wording changed several\n30\ttimes in 2026.\n31\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13b467b1-7ee4-4486-8fe8-6186fe1754a1","uuid":"3cedbe9a-59cc-4f65-bcaa-2e138c0a741b","timestamp":"2026-11-14T14:08:22.185Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/dev/Projects/kingfisher/README.md","content":"# kingfisher\n\nA local, browser-based live view of a coding agent at work. A Rust daemon on 127.0.0.1 owns the\nagent process, normalises its event stream, and feeds a WebGPU scene in a browser tab where one\ncan watch, chat back, interrupt, and approve permission requests.\n\nRuns Claude Code first, by spawning the unmodified official `claude` binary under the user's own\nlogin. kingfisher never reads, stores or forwards credentials. Other agents come later, through\nadapters.\n\n## Status\n\nDesign only. No code yet.\n\n- [docs/design-report.md](docs/design-report.md) is the founding research report (2026-11-14):\n  feasibility, integration paths, terms, prior art, rendering stack, architecture, MVP plan.\n\n## Plan\n\n| Milestone | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| Weekend MVP | Daemon spawns `claude -p` in bidirectional stream-json; `PermissionRequest` HTTP hook for approvals; cosmic scene, transcript panel, chat, interrupt; NDJSON archive and replay |\n| v0.2 | Global hooks plus transcript tail to observe hand-started sessions; take over via `--resume`; timeline, diff view, terminal pane, sonification; hang watchdog |\n| v0.3 | ACP and Codex adapters; multi-session; more themes; optional OTLP receiver |\n\n## Before any public release\n\nRe-read Anthropic's Claude Code legal page. The design relies on its carve-out for an end user\nsigning in to the unmodified binary with their own subscription, and that wording changed several\ntimes in 2026.\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013uMgogox2vspHDUdHUciuH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
